# Base change of the modular function field along ℚ↪ L

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange_modularFunctionField`
(`965445f6-eb6c-557d-834d-71e1f7ea99ac`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `506d7936-d4d7-5270-83b8-310c8cb62fbb`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $N$ be a nonzero natural
number. Inside the field $L((q))$ of Laurent series over $L$, consider two intermediate fields of
$L((q))/L$. The first is `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionField N)`: starting from the
intermediate field `modularFunctionField N` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))/\mathbb{Q}$ generated over
$\mathbb{Q}$ by the two elements `jq` and `qExpand ℚ N jq`, where `qExpand R N` is the ring
endomorphism of $R((q))$ obtained by multiplying all exponents by $N$ (substitution $q \mapsto
q^{N}$), one takes the image of this field under the coefficient embedding `coeffEmb L : ℚ((q)) →
L((q))` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, and adjoins that image to $L$. The second is
`modularFunctionFieldC L N`, the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by `jqModC L`, namely
$q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNum` with coefficients cast into $L$, together with `jqNModC L N =
qExpand L N (jqModC L)`. The assertion is that these two intermediate fields of $L((q))/L$ coincide.

This identifies the base change to $L$ of the two-generator modular function field $\mathbb{Q}(j(q),
j(q^{N})) \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ with the field $L(j(q), j(q^{N})) \subseteq L((q))$ generated
by the same $q$-expansions read with coefficients in $L$; no statement is made about the field
generated by $j(q^{d})$ for all divisors $d \mid N$. It serves as the compatibility step allowing
arguments about $X_0(N)$ and its function field to be transported from $\mathbb{Q}$ to an arbitrary
field of characteristic zero, and is used in the construction of fibre models on cusp charts and in
the study of the cuspidal divisor class.

